{"id": "EUVD-2026-108337", "enisaUuid": "a70fa638-68e3-31af-912f-a4d32eb172f3", "description": "libsmb2 before 6.3 contains integer overflow vulnerabilities in the DCE/RPC NDR decoder in lib/dcerpc.c that allow heap out-of-bounds reads and writes. A malicious SMB server or machine-in-the-middle on unsigned connections can send crafted NetrShareEnum replies with wrapping actual_count or max_count values when clients call smb2_share_enum_async(), corrupting heap memory.", "datePublished": "2026-10-22T19:14:05", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-22T19:14:05", "baseScore": 7.2, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:L/VI:L/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haindpwn/libsmb2-dcerpc-ndr-count-overflow-oob", "https://github.com/sahlberg/libsmb2/issues/496", "https://github.com/sahlberg/libsmb2/commit/a79f6914cb5ed3f74293d15cdea901261ce179ff", "https://github.com/sahlberg/libsmb2/releases/tag/libsmb2-6.3", "https://github.com/sahlberg/libsmb2", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/libsmb2-before-6.3-integer-overflow-in-dce-rpc-ndr-decoder-via-netrshareenum"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-115505", "GHSA-jfx5-c9g5-vf27"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "ddca328c-39b3-32e4-b755-25020524a4cb", "product": {"name": "libsmb2", "vendor": {"name": "sahlberg"}}, "product_version": "0 <6.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "7cc557e8-7a03-3823-99eb-91d0ad0cf3f8", "vendor": {"name": "sahlberg"}}], "isExploited": false}